# Pause That

Read `docs/pause-that-build-spec.md` before writing any screen. It is the contract. When it conflicts with `docs/NATIVE-V1-SCOPE.md`, `docs/SHUTDOWN-INTERACTION-SPEC.md`, or `docs/PRODUCT-V1-CANON.md`, the build spec wins.

Non-negotiable:

1. The worse the user feels, the less the app should ask from them.
2. No timers, ever visible. No duration picker, no countdown, no "back on in 30 minutes," no "Overthinking is back on" message. A switch that was turned off quietly becomes available again later. The reset is silent. This includes Shutdown. Do not reintroduce durations, expirations, or remaining-time displays in code, tests, docs, or comments.
3. No engagement mechanics. No streaks, guilt notifications, scores, dashboards, or badges.
4. "That's enough" always ends the interaction. At most three follow-ups, and one is always "That's enough."
5. Laugh with the user, never at the user.
6. No clinical claims. Do not say therapy, treatment, disorder, or promise outcomes.
7. Hold This never resurfaces on its own.
8. Haptics reinforce, never carry. Every haptic has a visual twin.

Do not commit a rework diff until the founder's design agent has reviewed it against the mockup and this spec.
